                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a fish, to walk along the seafloor using its fins as limbs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "punt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13e6f205-a4be-35e9-b546-c1e168763829",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dropkick; to kick something a considerable distance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d47aff1b-4af0-40ca-bb41-a5a4be12de9b",
                                                "sense_id": "13e6f205-a4be-35e9-b546-c1e168763829",
                                                "text": "At the dump he emptied the station wagon quickly and only once punted a bag of refuse, exploding it like a pinata at a Mexican Christmas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "913b1d1a-a35a-437a-b723-76870e8e8170",
                                                "sense_id": "13e6f205-a4be-35e9-b546-c1e168763829",
                                                "text": "He even hated pets—I once saw him punt a cat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0364b044-4ba1-3623-8397-63b0ce0c3e7e",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dropkick; to kick something a considerable distance.",
                                            "To kick a ball dropped from the hands before it hits the ground. (This puts the ball farther from the goal across which the opposing team is attempting to score, so improves the chances of the team punting.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f36756e2-ecde-3a9c-bf05-7ce47c9d7fa2",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To dropkick; to kick something a considerable distance.",
                                            "To kick a bouncing ball far and high."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32995ae2-ca94-451b-8798-df5fad6d9dac",
                                                "sense_id": "f36756e2-ecde-3a9c-bf05-7ce47c9d7fa2",
                                                "text": "With five minutes remaining Hennessey was down well to block another Vukcevic shot, while Gunter was smartly in to punt away the dangerous loose ball."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4946ee9e-2a70-3149-8c9a-3178f1dc22fc",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To equivocate and delay or put off (answering a question, addressing an issue, etc)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc3103c2-b110-464b-a00e-f381bc7c9c28",
                                                "sense_id": "4946ee9e-2a70-3149-8c9a-3178f1dc22fc",
                                                "text": "The briefer reported it had been terminated on orders from Secretary Schlesinger, but attributed this to a sense Shamrock produced little, not to the fact it had been discovered. The NSA briefer punted on whether Fort Meade had been reading Americans' private messages, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e79133c4-7f4b-434d-93aa-4b11e653a211",
                                                "sense_id": "4946ee9e-2a70-3149-8c9a-3178f1dc22fc",
                                                "text": "The federal government has punted bringing forward extraordinary immigration powers that just weeks ago it was saying were so urgent they needed to be rushed through the parliament."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "817dc24e-0652-3cfe-9b33-5a3f31f90362",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To retreat from one's objective; to abandon an effort one still notionally supports."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09457cca-639e-4f49-a5be-c4242ce1bd4b",
                                                "sense_id": "817dc24e-0652-3cfe-9b33-5a3f31f90362",
                                                "text": "Punting: Using svn revert¶ If you decide that you want to throw out your changes and start your edits again (whether this occurs after a conflict or anytime), just revert your changes"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0832ef3-61b1-3f32-8b43-d824a0a38a5d",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make the best choice from a set of non-ideal alternatives."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1be80b9-4ac7-3f37-84ac-f0fb178021c1",
                                        "entry_id": "8bbb9d56-efdd-38bc-9624-4d48bdac6957",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To eject; to kick out of a place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20884fd3-3112-4bde-9909-f46ece040197",
                                                "sense_id": "a1be80b9-4ac7-3f37-84ac-f0fb178021c1",
                                                "text": "The user is punted from the channel, and must rejoin to gain access."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7f7ffe3-c60b-4c03-9288-97de0e9ee722",
                                                "sense_id": "a1be80b9-4ac7-3f37-84ac-f0fb178021c1",
                                                "text": "If you want to join this riot, we urge you to! You wont have to worry about being TOSed or reported because there will be no Guides online! So do whatever you want—punt, scroll, tos, just turn AOL into a war zone!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
